  "notes": "Specifically refers to school club activities ({部活|ぶかつ}). In Japanese schools, students typically choose a club to join at the start of the school year.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {入部|にゅうぶ}{届|とどけ} (club membership application form)\n- {入部|にゅうぶ}{希望|きぼう} (desire to join a club)\n- {入部|にゅうぶ}テスト (tryout for joining a club)\n- ～{部|ぶ}に{入部|にゅうぶ}する (join the ~ club)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {退部|たいぶ}: quitting a club\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {入会|にゅうかい}: joining an organization (broader — gyms, associations, etc.)\n- {入団|にゅうだん}: joining a team or troupe (sports teams, theater groups)",
